title: Input history
tags: GUI
kind: guide
aliases: input-history recall ctrl-p ctrl-n ctrl-r
summary: Each text zone remembers what was submitted in it, per repository: `ctrl+p` and `ctrl+n` walk back and forth, `ctrl+r` searches.

The text zones keep what was submitted in them, ''per repository and per zone''.
Four zones have a history:

* the command input in command mode, and in bash mode — two separate histories ([[The command input]], [[Bash mode]]);
* the finder and the query of `metarecord-list`.

!! Recalling

|!Key |!Does |
|`ctrl+p` / `ctrl+n` |the previous / the next entry, as in a terminal. What was being typed is kept at the newest end and comes back when walking past it. |
|`ctrl+r` |a search box over the entries: newest first, each shown once, narrowed by the pieces typed, in order. `ctrl+p` / `ctrl+n` or the arrows choose, `Enter` puts the entry in the zone, `Escape` — or clicking elsewhere — gives up. |

Editing the recalled text ends the walk: the edited text is the new draft. Leaving
the zone ends it too, so the first `ctrl+p` after coming back recalls the newest
entry again.

These three keys belong to the zones themselves and are not in `keybindings.toml` ([[Keybindings]]).
Binding `ctrl+p`, `ctrl+n` or `ctrl+r` there with `text-input = true` would take
them over.

!! What is recorded

An entry is recorded when the zone is ''submitted'' — `Enter`, or the command that
applies it — never while typing. The command mode records what actually ran: the
command chosen in the list, not the few letters typed to reach it. An answer to a
question — a command's argument, a script's prompt — is not recorded.

Submitting the same text twice in a row records it once. Each zone keeps its 1000
newest entries.

In a workspace without a repository the history still works, but lasts the session
only; it is not carried into a repository's history when one is opened.

!! Where it is kept

In the repository: one plain-text file per zone,
`.metafolder/gui/history/<zone>` — `shell:command`, `shell:bash`,
`metarecord-list:finder`, `metarecord-list:query` — one entry per line, the newest
last. The file is replaced whole at each addition (written aside, then renamed), so
an interrupted write leaves the previous history intact.

These files are ordinary content of `.metafolder/`, unlike `internal/`: they can be
tracked, and are in practice ignored by the `.metafolder` pattern every repository
starts with ([[Repository layout on disk]]).

The GUI reads and writes them itself; the daemon has no part in it and no endpoint
for it. It finds the repository's `.metafolder/` from `GET /repos`, which is right
also when that directory lives outside the root. A panel reaches its own zones
through `metafolder.history.read` and `metafolder.history.append`, and the keys
through `attachHistory` of `/__history.js`. A zone's name is made of lowercase
letters, digits, `:`, `_` and `-`, 64 at most, so it cannot name a file outside the
history directory.
